{"signature": "{\"text\": \"Hydroelectric stations use water stored at height. As the water flows downhill, its gravitational potential energy store decreases and energy is transferred to the kinetic energy stores of the moving water and turbine, then electrically through a generator. Hydroelectric generation can be controllable where reservoirs are available, but dams may be costly and may flood habitats or settlements. Tidal systems exploit the predictable movement of seawater caused by tides. Tidal barrages and tidal-stream turbines can generate electricity, but suitable locations are limited and marine ecosystems may be affected.\", \"voice\": \"en-NG-AbeoNeural\", \"rate\": \"-4%\", \"eleven\": true}", "duration": 43.049796, "words": [["Hydroelectric", 0.0], ["stations", 0.906], ["use", 1.625], ["water", 1.95], ["stored", 2.322], ["at", 2.682], ["height.", 2.844], ["As", 3.68], ["the", 4.063], ["water", 4.238], ["flows", 4.609], ["downhill,", 4.981], ["its", 5.921], ["gravitational", 6.2], ["potential", 6.978], ["energy", 7.581], ["store", 8.034], ["decreases", 8.348], ["and", 9.311], ["energy", 9.752], ["is", 10.356], ["transferred", 10.565], ["to", 11.366], ["the", 11.587], ["kinetic", 11.726], ["energy", 12.307], ["stores", 12.759], ["of", 13.386], ["the", 13.642], ["moving", 13.793], ["water", 14.187], ["and", 14.605], ["turbine,", 14.814], ["then", 15.766], ["electrically", 16.161], ["through", 16.939], ["a", 17.322], ["generator.", 17.473], ["Hydroelectric", 18.39], ["generation", 19.237], ["can", 20.004], ["be", 20.306], ["controllable", 20.468], ["where", 21.281], ["reservoirs", 21.559], ["are", 22.198], ["available,", 22.395], ["but", 23.301], ["dams", 23.556], ["may", 24.032], ["be", 24.23], ["costly", 24.381], ["and", 25.263], ["may", 25.553], ["flood", 25.785], ["habitats", 26.134], ["or", 26.923], ["settlements.", 27.121], ["Tidal", 28.282], ["systems", 28.758], ["exploit", 29.419], ["the", 30.07], ["predictable", 30.209], ["movement", 30.929], ["o